s to know about!</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://reddit.com/r/DataIsBeautiful\">/r/DataIsBeautiful</a></li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Getting Help: Questions, Answers, Chats</h2><h3>Some communities to know about!</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://reddit.com/r/DataScience\">/r/DataScience</a></li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Getting Help: Questions, Answers, Chats</h2><h3>Some communities to know about!</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://stats.stackexchange.com/\">Cross-Validated: stats.stackexchange.com</a></li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Getting Help: Questions, Answers, Chats</h2><h3>Some communities to know about!</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ossu/data-science#:~:text=Discord%20server\"><code>ossu/data-science</code> has a Discord server and newsletter</a></li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Skilling up</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong>Ask a question. Start exploring some data.</strong> The <a href=\"https://github.com/DataScienceSpecialization/courses/blob/master/01_DataScientistToolbox/03_02_whatIsData/index.Rmd#the-data-is-the-second-most-important-thing\">\"most important thing in data science is the question\"</a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/jtleek\">Dr. Jeff T. Leek</a>). So start with a question. Then, find <a href=\"https://github.com/caesar0301/awesome-public-datasets\">real data</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/caesar0301/awesome-public-datasets\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">47.6k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":47617,\"repo\":\"caesar0301/awesome-public-datasets\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->. Analyze it. Then ...</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Skilling up</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong>Communicate results.</strong> When you think you have a novel finding, ask for review. When you're still learning, ask in informal communities (some are <a href=\"#some-communities-to-know-about\">linked below</a>).</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Skilling up</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong>Learn from feedback.</strong> Consider <a href=\"https://www.swyx.io/learn-in-public/\">learning in public</a>, it works great for some folks. (Don't pressure yourself yet though! Everybody is different, and it's good to know your learning style.)</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More ways to \"Dive into Machine Learning\"</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong>2022:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/rasbt/machine-learning-book\"><em>Machine Learning with PyTorch and Scikit-Learn</em> by Sebastian Raschka, Yuxi (Hayden) Liu, and Vahid Mirjalili</a></li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-26T05:40:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"rothgar/awesome-tmux","categoryHTML":"<h2>Status Bar</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ofirgall/tmux-window-name\">tmux-window-name</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/ofirgall/tmux-window-name\"